<title>HONG KONG: Peregrine fails in plan to privatise unit.</title>
<headline>Peregrine fails in plan to privatise unit.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The plan of Hong Kong-based investment bank Peregrine Investments Holdings Ltd to privatise its property unit Kwong Sang Hong International Ltd has lapsed, the two companies said in a joint statement on Wednesday.</p>
<p>At a court meeting convened by the direction of the Supreme Court held on Wednesday, the number of shareholders who voted in favour of the privatisation proposal was below the requisite majority, the statement said.</p>
<p>Shares in both companies were suspended on Wednesday.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6590</p>
</text>
